# Call-site ledger of websocket-client at 12225f5ce6e27536be3b0da85fd763ed75581bcc.
# Decide every `undecided` line; see macro-benchmark/README.md.
#
# The scope rules A, B1-B5 and C are in macro-benchmark/README.md;
# websocket-client.md shows how this ledger applies them. Sockets: the
# package's own sockets are socket.socket (_http._open_socket) and
# ssl.SSLSocket (ssl.SSLContext.wrap_socket in _http._wrap_sni_socket). The
# client's pre-initialised socket (the `socket` option) is socket.socket by
# its annotation and documentation (B4; websocket-client.md J3). The socket that python-socks returns
# (_http._start_proxied_socket) is a value of a missing module: see
# websocket-client.md, J3.
default reject websocket._core.WebSocket.__iter__, websocket._core.WebSocket.__next__: no WebSocket object is iterated, unpacked, searched with `in` or passed to a builtin that iterates (sum, any, sorted, filter, map, list, join) at this site; the iterated values are lists, tuples, dicts and their views, strs, bytes, generator expressions, addrinfo lists, cookie values or client collections (sockopt, no_proxy, subprotocols, header), never the WebSocket that create_connection or WebSocketApp makes (WebSocket.next accepts __next__ explicitly)
default reject websocket._abnf.ABNF.__str__: no formatted, %-converted or str()-converted value at this site is an ABNF frame; the values are ints, strs, bytes reprs, exceptions, lists, dicts, None or client values (the explicit frame.__str__() calls in WebSocket.send_frame and recv_data_frame, and the f-strings of run_forever.handleDisconnect at _app.py:583 and 591, J5, accept it)
default reject websocket._cookiejar.SimpleCookieJar.get: the receiver of this .get call is a dict (options, sslopt, headers, kwargs), os.environ, a http.cookies.Morsel, a client object or ABNF.OPCODE_MAP, never a SimpleCookieJar; the one SimpleCookieJar receiver is the module-level CookieJar in _handshake._get_handshake_headers, which accepts it

